NNOOTTEESS
     The bar is an ordinary window: other windows may cover it,
     and a left click on it raises it again.  It cannot be hid-
     den, moved or resized, takes no keyboard focus, and does not
     appear in the desktop menu's SSwwiittcchh ttoo...  list.

     The dock matches windows to catalog entries by window title:
     an application's declared title must equal its catalog name
     (the convention throughout the shipped catalog), or its icon
     will not read as running.  The state of the bar follows the
     desktop immediately: the server notifies the dock the moment
     the window list changes.  (A launch that dies before it
     makes a window is noticed by a slower fallback poll, so its
     icon may stay pressed for a couple of seconds.)
